<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francisco Ramírez</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1786–1821</span> · Also known as Pancho Ramírez</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francisco Ramírez was a caudillo of Entre Ríos and a lieutenant of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-gervasio-artigas">José Gervasio Artigas</a> in the Federal League. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estanislao-lopez">Estanislao López</a> he defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a> at Cepeda in 1820 and signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-pilar">Treaty of Pilar</a>, then turned on Artigas and drove him into exile. He set up the Republic of Entre Ríos but was killed in July 1821 during a campaign against Santa Fe and Buenos Aires.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francisco-ramirez.jpg" alt="Francisco Ramírez" width="320" height="372" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 43K2Mühle · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Francisco_Ramirez_2_(cropped).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
